        <!-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
             5. MALAYSIA — EPF / SOCSO PACKAGE
             Mandatory contributions under Malaysian Labour Law.
             EPF Employee: 11% of gross (employees below 60).
             SOCSO Employee: 0.5% of gross (capped at MYR 86.65/month).
             EIS Employee: 0.4% of gross (Employment Insurance System).
             PCB/MTD (income tax withholding): add per employee individually.
        ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
        <record id="tmpl_malaysia" model="dotbd.salary.template">
            <field name="name">Malaysia — EPF / SOCSO Standard Package</field>
            <field name="template_type">malaysia</field>
            <field name="working_days_per_month">22</field>
            <field name="note">
Compliant with Malaysian Employment Act 1955 and statutory contribution requirements.
EPF (KWSP): Employee 11%, Employer 13% for salary ≤ MYR 5,000 (12% for higher).
  Enable/disable per employee age group (employees over 60 contribute 5.5%).
SOCSO (PERKESO): Employee 0.5%, capped at maximum insurable earnings.
  Disable for employees earning above RM 4,000/month (employer pays only).
EIS (SIP): Employee 0.4%, employer 0.4%, capped at RM 4,000 insurable earnings.
PCB/MTD (Income Tax): add as individual fixed deduction per employee slab.
Overtime: calculated per Employment Act (1.5x hourly rate) — track separately.
Working days: 22 (standard 5-day week; adjust for 5.5 or 6-day operations).
            </field>
        </record>

        <record id="comp_mys_hra" model="dotbd.salary.component">
            <field name="template_id" ref="tmpl_malaysia"/>
            <field name="sequence">10</field>
            <field name="name">Housing Allowance</field>
            <field name="code">HRA</field>
            <field name="component_type">allowance</field>
            <field name="calculation_type">percentage</field>
            <field name="percentage">20</field>
        </record>
        <record id="comp_mys_transport" model="dotbd.salary.component">
            <field name="template_id" ref="tmpl_malaysia"/>
            <field name="sequence">20</field>
            <field name="name">Transport Allowance</field>
            <field name="code">TRN</field>
            <field name="component_type">allowance</field>
            <field name="calculation_type">percentage</field>
            <field name="percentage">10</field>
        </record>
        <record id="comp_mys_epf" model="dotbd.salary.component">
            <field name="template_id" ref="tmpl_malaysia"/>
            <field name="sequence">30</field>
            <field name="name">EPF — Employee Contribution (11%)</field>
            <field name="code">EPF_EMP</field>
            <field name="component_type">deduction</field>
            <field name="calculation_type">percentage</field>
            <field name="percentage">11</field>
        </record>
        <record id="comp_mys_socso" model="dotbd.salary.component">
            <field name="template_id" ref="tmpl_malaysia"/>
            <field name="sequence">40</field>
            <field name="name">SOCSO — Employee Contribution (0.5%)</field>
            <field name="code">SOCSO_EMP</field>
            <field name="component_type">deduction</field>
            <field name="calculation_type">percentage</field>
            <field name="percentage">0.5</field>
        </record>
        <record id="comp_mys_eis" model="dotbd.salary.component">
            <field name="template_id" ref="tmpl_malaysia"/>
            <field name="sequence">50</field>
            <field name="name">EIS — Employee Contribution (0.4%)</field>
            <field name="code">EIS_EMP</field>
            <field name="component_type">deduction</field>
            <field name="calculation_type">percentage</field>
            <field name="percentage">0.4</field>
        </record>

        <record id="lvrule_mys_unpaid" model="dotbd.salary.leave.rule">
            <field name="template_id" ref="tmpl_malaysia"/>
            <field name="sequence">99</field>
            <field name="name">No Pay Leave Deduction</field>
            <field name="rule_action">deduct</field>
            <field name="amount_type">per_day_gross</field>
        </record>

        <!-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
             6. PHILIPPINES — SSS / PHILHEALTH / PAG-IBIG PACKAGE
             Mandatory contributions under Philippine Labour Code.
             SSS: employee share ~4.5% of Monthly Salary Credit (MSC).
             PhilHealth: employee 2.5% of basic (effective 2024).
             Pag-IBIG (HDMF): PHP 100 fixed or 2% of basic (max PHP 100 voluntary).
             Tax (BIR): withholding tax; add per employee as fixed deduction.
        ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
        <record id="tmpl_philippines" model="dotbd.salary.template">
            <field name="name">Philippines — SSS / PhilHealth / Pag-IBIG Package</field>
            <field name="template_type">philippines</field>
            <field name="working_days_per_month">22</field>
            <field name="note">
Compliant with Philippine Labour Code mandatory contribution requirements (2024).
SSS: Employee contribution based on Monthly Salary Credit table (~4.5% effective rate).
  The fixed component here is PHP 450 as an approximation for PHP 10,000 basic.
  Adjust the fixed amount per the SSS contribution table for each salary range.
PhilHealth: Employee 2.5% of basic salary (effective 2024, up to PHP 5,000/month).
Pag-IBIG (HDMF): PHP 100/month mandatory minimum (or 2% if employee opts for higher).
BIR Withholding Tax: add per employee as individual fixed deduction.
13th Month Pay: 1/12 of basic per month (mandatory); include here or pay separately.
COLA (Cost of Living Allowance): may be applicable under DOLE orders — add if required.
            </field>
        </record>

