        <!-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
             7. INDONESIA — BPJS PACKAGE
             Mandatory BPJS Ketenagakerjaan (social security) and
             BPJS Kesehatan (health insurance) contributions.
             JHT (Jaminan Hari Tua): employee 2% of salary.
             JP (Jaminan Pensiun): employee 1% of salary.
             BPJS Kesehatan: employee 1% of salary (capped at IDR 12M salary).
             PPh 21 (income tax): add per employee individually.
        ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
        <record id="tmpl_indonesia" model="dotbd.salary.template">
            <field name="name">Indonesia — BPJS Standard Package</field>
            <field name="template_type">indonesia</field>
            <field name="working_days_per_month">22</field>
            <field name="note">
Compliant with Indonesian Manpower Law (UU Ketenagakerjaan) and BPJS requirements.
BPJS Ketenagakerjaan:
  - JHT (Old Age Security): Employee 2%, Employer 3.7%
  - JP (Pension): Employee 1%, Employer 2% (capped at JPY 9,559,600 annual salary)
  - JKK (Accident Insurance): Employer only (0.24–1.74%) — not deducted from employee
  - JKM (Death Insurance): Employer only (0.3%) — not deducted from employee
BPJS Kesehatan (Health): Employee 1% of salary, Employer 4% (capped at IDR 12M/month).
PPh 21 (Income Tax): varies by slab; add as fixed deduction per employee.
THR (Tunjangan Hari Raya / Holiday Bonus): 1 month salary paid before Lebaran.
  Provision monthly at 8.33% or pay directly in the holiday month.
Meal and transport allowances are common — included here as fixed amounts.
            </field>
